[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1789","stub":{"id":"1789","section":"Suck Confluence to Bridge","altname":"","river":"Suck Creek","difficulty":"IVtoVplus","states":["USA-TNN"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":null,"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"112470","location":{"latitude":"35.1454238891602","longitude":"-85.388427734375"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"This rapid was once a sweet boof it has now collapsed on itself to form a broken slide that currently has some wood in it. It will continue to change as the shale that forms it is eroded away during each flood event.","id":"8201","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Shitty Shitty Bang Bang","distance":"0.2","difficulty":"IV+","approximate":false,"photoID":"17926"},{"type":"rapid","description":"This rapid has changed several times. Once a fast steep slide and one of the biggest rapids on the run it is now a low angle slide with some large trees in the river.","id":"1689","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Optimus Prime","distance":"0.3","difficulty":"V","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"rapid","description":"A double drop with several different entrances. The entrances have several pin spots.\nThere are two main lines. The river left, where the old sieve used to be and right of center.\nThere is a submerged rock on the right at the bottom and a large exposed rock on the left.\nScout from river right along the concrete wall.","id":"1690","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Road Construction","distance":"0.4","difficulty":"V","approximate":false,"photoID":"7880"},{"type":"rapid","description":"This is the site of a pin that resulted in a drowning. It has since changed but is still dangerous. There is an old jeep trail that accesses the creek at this point.\nThe best line is to thread an S move between the holes for the final slide boof.","id":"8202","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Razor's Edge","distance":"0.5","difficulty":"IV+","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"rapid","description":"After a trashy entrance you can enter this three part drop on the left or right. Finishing with a nice boof.","id":"1691","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Slow and Low","distance":"0.6","difficulty":"V","approximate":false,"photoID":"14227"},{"type":"waterfall","description":"At higher levels a hole and recirculating eddy forms.","id":"1492","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Pinnacle","distance":"0.8","difficulty":"V","approximate":false,"photoID":"7864"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Shallow Slide to Boof in the main channel\nHigher water opens up a slide line on the right and an interesting boof through a crack.","id":"1693","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Velcro Zipper","distance":"0.9","difficulty":"IV+","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"rapid","description":"Double drop with a trashy exit","id":"1694","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Sheit Bird Alley","distance":"0.95","difficulty":"V","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"rapid","description":"An easy boof at most levels. At higher water it has lead to inadvertent cartwheels by even the most skilled boaters. This drop is just below Shit Bird Alley and just above the gauge and Knuckle Head. This rapid is named after Stan Guy.","id":"8198","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Stan's Rapid","distance":"1","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false,"photoID":"17562"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Take out above this one or continue downstream to the bridge. One of the largest most challenging drops on the run.","id":"1695","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Knuckle Head","distance":"1.1","difficulty":"V+","approximate":false,"photoID":"17528"},{"type":"rapid","description":"One of the most complex rapids on the run.\nThe landing zone has a large rock you must avoid landing your boat or body on.","id":"1696","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Beyond Thunderdome","distance":"1.2","difficulty":"V+","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"rapid","description":"One of the larger rapids on the lower stretch.\nThe entrance slide has a sticky hole with an eddy that feeds back into the hole from there the paddler must choose to go left or right of the large boulder. Depending on water level one side is better than the other. There is a high pin potential on the left at lower levels, at higher levels the pin rocks get covered and the left is more open.","id":"8199","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Hamburger (AKA Lane Brain)","distance":"1.5","difficulty":"V","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"rapid","description":"A fun series of ledges near the takeout. One of the longest rapids of the run. The fun factor increases with the water level.","id":"8200","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Cooler Rapid","distance":"1.9","difficulty":"IV+","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"117755","location":{"latitude":"35.1242179870605","longitude":"-85.3902053833008"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"2","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"100147121","title":null,"post_date":"2007-12-27 05:00:00+00","detail":"New guard rails have been placed in the pull offs along Suck Creek. Please try and share a ride to the creek as parking is now very limited, take caution when utilizing and pulling into and out of the small pull offs.","user":null}],"photos":[{"id":"14298","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8484","description":"","caption":"Road Construction","poi_name":"road construction","subject":"andy","author":"Jared seiler","poi_id":"1690","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14298","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.or